---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/data/site";
const updated = "5 September 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy notice | MyWebMaster"
  description="How MyWebMaster collects and uses personal data: what we hold, why we hold it, how long we keep it, and the rights you have under UK GDPR."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Privacy", href: "/legal/privacy/" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="mono muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} ("we") operates {site.domain}. For the purposes of UK data protection law we
        are the data controller for personal data collected through this website. You can reach
        us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you send us.</strong> If you request a scan, we collect the name,
          email address, website address and any message you provide.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Aggregate usage data.</strong> We use privacy-respecting analytics to count
          page views and referrers. We do not use advertising cookies, and we do not build
          profiles of individual visitors.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host records requests, including IP address and user
          agent, for security and to identify which crawlers fetch our pages.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use the details you send to run the scan you asked for and to reply to you. Our lawful
        basis is legitimate interests — responding to an enquiry you initiated. We use aggregate
        usage data to understand which pages are useful, on the same basis.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data, we do not share it with advertising networks, and we do not
        send marketing email to people who have not asked for it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry correspondence is kept for two years from the last contact, then deleted. Server
        logs are retained for a shorter period by our hosting provider.
      </p>

      <h2>Client data</h2>
      <p>
        Where we operate Autopilot on a client's website, we access that client's Google Search
        Console and analytics data under their instruction. In that arrangement the client is the
        controller and we are the processor, governed by the contract between us.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to
        correct or delete it, or object to our processing. Email us and we will respond within
        one month. If you are unhappy with our response you can complain to the Information
        Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-block: 1rem 0.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2.2em; }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
